r-line px-5 py-4" aria-labelledby="sec-ask" data-testid="ask"><h2 id="sec-ask" class="eyebrow mb-3">Ask the evidence</h2><div><form class="flex gap-2"><label for="ask-input" class="sr-only">Ask a question about the evidence</label><input id="ask-input" class="field" placeholder="Has a solid ever burned near 8.2 psi?" autocomplete="off" value=""><button type="submit" class="btn">Ask</button></form><div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2" aria-label="Questions with checked answers" data-prompt=""><button type="button" class="chip h-auto whitespace-normal py-1 text-left text-xs" aria-pressed="false">What fire tests exist near 8.2 psi and 34% oxygen?</button><button type="button" class="chip h-auto whitespace-normal py-1 text-left text-xs" aria-pressed="false">If NASA has already burned fabric in near-Moon-base air, why can't a researcher download it?</button><button type="button" class="chip h-auto whitespace-normal py-1 text-left text-xs" aria-pressed="false">Has a solid material ever been burned near a candidate Moon-base atmosphere?</button><button type="button" class="chip h-auto whitespace-normal py-1 text-left text-xs" aria-pressed="false">Why can't the ACME BRE data be placed on the trade map?</button><button type="button" class="chip h-auto whitespace-normal py-1 text-left text-xs" aria-pressed="false">What did FLEX show about carbon dioxide suppression near 10.4 psi?</button><button type="button" class="chip h-auto whitespace-normal py-1 text-left text-xs" aria-pressed="false">Which atmosphere should NASA choose for the Moon base?</button><button type="button" class="chip h-auto whitespace-normal py-1 text-left text-xs" aria-pressed="false">Is there partial-gravity fire data for the Moon?</button></div><div aria-live="polite" class="mt-4"></div></div></section><p class="border-t border-line px-5 py-4 text-xs text-ink-3">Redshift informs a decision; it does not rank or recommend an atmosphere. Empty means unknown, never safe.</p><div class="sticky bottom-0 z-10 m